{%- comment -%}
  Collection - the completed residences only (For Sale has its own page;
  sold and completed are the same thing here). From the page header down:
  an intro band (label, "Completed residences, N and counting", one line
  in the Sabdia voice, the suburbs present), then a filter bar that sticks
  under the nav, then one editorial grid of photo tiles. Films belong on
  each residence's own page; "Film on hover" is there as a dial only.

  Each Residence block points at the residence's page (Content › Pages,
  template "collection-item"); its name, location, style, completed
  year, photo and film all come from that page's metafields, so a page
  edited in Pages updates the card too. The block's own fields only
  override.

  Sticky bar (11 Sep 2026): the nav is 80px tall at the top of the page
  and 68px once scrolled (60 / 56 on phones), so a bar pinned at
  top: var(--nav-h) sat 12px below the scrolled nav with the tiles
  showing through the strip. The bar now measures the nav (ResizeObserver
  on #mainNav) and pins itself to its live height.

  Scale: with twenty or more residences the style chips and suburb list
  are still deduplicated from every block, and "Show more" (off by
  default) keeps the first N tiles on the page and reveals the rest on a
  button, no reload; filters always search the whole set.
  Filters (15 Sep 2026): Style and Suburb sit side by side at the left of
  the bar, each a dropdown with a tick box beside every choice (the For
  Sale Features menu, in this bar's own type), so several can be chosen. A
  residence shows when its style is one of the ticked styles (or none is
  ticked) and its suburb one of the ticked suburbs (or none is). Both lists
  hold every style and suburb of the cards on the page, once each, A to Z.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sid = section.id
  assign pcount = 0
  assign empty_blocks = 0
  assign count_token = '{' | append: 'count' | append: '}'
  # Switched off for launch (10 Sep 2026): For Sale has its own page. Turn
  # "Include residences from Products" on and the current homes lead the
  # grid again, tagged For Sale / Sold, with matching filter choices.
  assign show_current = section.settings.show_current
  assign scope = section.settings.current_scope | default: 'all'
  assign current_handles = '' | split: ','
  if show_current
    if scope == 'all'
      capture live_csv
        render 'residence-handles', col: collections['for-sale'], group: 'live'
      endcapture
      assign live_handles = live_csv | split: ','
      assign current_handles = current_handles | concat: live_handles
    endif
    capture sold_csv
      render 'residence-handles', col: collections['sold'], group: 'sold'
    endcapture
    assign sold_handles = sold_csv | split: ','
    assign current_handles = current_handles | concat: sold_handles
  endif
  assign tile_media = section.settings.tile_media | default: 'photo'
  assign more_after = 0
  if section.settings.show_more
    assign more_after = section.settings.show_more_after | default: 12
  endif
  assign live_word = section.settings.filter_live | default: 'For Sale'
  assign sold_word = section.settings.filter_sold | default: 'Sold'
  assign has_live = false
  assign has_sold = false
  assign suburbs_raw = ''
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  The homes from Products lead the grid, so their cards are written here,
  ahead of the filter bar, and printed at the top of the grid below: that
  way their suburbs and For Sale / Sold groups reach the filter lists.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture current_cards -%}
  {%- if show_current -%}
    {%- for h in current_handles -%}
      {%- for product in collections.all.products -%}
        {%- if product.handle != h -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- capture pstatus -%}{% render 'residence-status', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign grp = live_word
          if pstatus contains 'Sold'
            assign grp = sold_word
            assign has_sold = true
          else
            assign has_live = true
          endif
          assign p_suburb = product.metafields.custom.suburb.value | split: ',' | first | replace: ' QLD', '' | replace: ' Qld', '' | strip
          if p_suburb != blank
            assign suburbs_raw = suburbs_raw | append: p_suburb | append: '¦'
          endif
          assign pcount = pcount | plus: 1
        -%}
            <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="pf-card reveal{% if more_after > 0 and pcount > more_after %} pf-more{% endif %}" data-port-card data-style="{{ grp | escape }}" data-suburb="{{ p_suburb | escape }}">
              {%- if product.featured_image -%}
              <div class="pf-media">
                  <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200, height: 900, crop: 'center' }}" alt="{{ product.title | escape }}" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                <span class="port-film-tag">{{ pstatus }}</span>
              </div>
              {%- endif -%}
              <div class="pf-info">
                <div class="pf-name">{% render 'residence-name', product: product %} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></div>
                <div class="pf-meta">{{ product.metafields.custom.suburb.value }}{% if product.metafields.custom.year.value != blank %} <i>&middot;</i> {{ product.metafields.custom.year.value }}{% endif %}</div>
              </div>
            </a>
        {%- break -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  # Every Style and Suburb choice comes from a card that is on the page
  # (Naomi, 15 Sep 2026: "ensure that all of the styles and suburbs are
  # placed"). Each block is read through the same fields its card reads;
  # a block with no residence, name or photo is left out of the grid, so
  # it is neither counted nor listed.
  assign styles_raw = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    assign rp = block.settings.page
    if rp == blank and block.settings.link contains '/pages/'
      assign rp_handle = block.settings.link | split: '/pages/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '#' | first
      assign rp = pages[rp_handle]
    endif
    if block.settings.product == blank and rp.title == blank and block.settings.name == blank and block.settings.image == blank and block.settings.image_ext == blank
      assign empty_blocks = empty_blocks | plus: 1
      continue
    endif
    if block.settings.product != blank
      assign r_style = block.settings.style | default: block.settings.product.metafields.custom.style.value | strip
      assign r_loc = block.settings.loc | default: block.settings.product.metafields.custom.suburb.value
    else
      assign r_style = block.settings.style | default: rp.metafields.custom.style.value | strip
      assign r_loc = block.settings.loc | default: rp.metafields.custom.loc.value
    endif
    assign r_suburb = r_loc | split: ',' | first | replace: ' QLD', '' | replace: ' Qld', '' | strip
    if r_style != blank
      assign styles_raw = styles_raw | append: r_style | append: '¦'
    endif
    if r_suburb != blank
      assign suburbs_raw = suburbs_raw | append: r_suburb | append: '¦'
    endif
  endfor
  # One entry per value whatever its capitals or spacing ("Camp Hill" and
  # "camp  hill" are one suburb; the first spelling met is shown), A to Z.
  assign seen = '¦'
  assign kept = ''
  assign list_in = styles_raw | split: '¦'
  for v in list_in
    assign vv = v | split: ' ' | join: ' '
    assign v_key = vv | downcase | prepend: '¦' | append: '¦'
    if vv == blank or seen contains v_key
      continue
    endif
    assign seen = seen | append: v_key
    assign kept = kept | append: vv | append: '¦'
  endfor
  assign styles = kept | split: '¦' | sort_natural
  assign seen = '¦'
  assign kept = ''
  assign list_in = suburbs_raw | split: '¦'
  for v in list_in
    assign vv = v | split: ' ' | join: ' '
    assign v_key = vv | downcase | prepend: '¦' | append: '¦'
    if vv == blank or seen contains v_key
      continue
    endif
    assign seen = seen | append: v_key
    assign kept = kept | append: vv | append: '¦'
  endfor
  assign suburbs = kept | split: '¦' | sort_natural
  assign total = section.blocks.size | minus: empty_blocks
  if show_current
    assign total = total | plus: current_handles.size
  endif
  assign show_lead = true
  if section.settings.show_lead == false
    assign show_lead = false
  endif
  assign lead_heading = section.settings.lead_heading
  if lead_heading == blank
    assign lead_heading = 'Completed residences, <em>' | append: count_token | append: ' and counting</em>.'
  endif
  assign lead_heading = lead_heading | replace: count_token, total
-%}

{% render 'residence-faces' %}
{% render 'section-look', section: section %}
{%- if show_lead -%}
<section class="pf-lead" id="pfLead-{{ sid }}">
  <div class="inner pf-lead-grid">
    <div class="pf-lead-a">
      {%- if section.settings.lead_label != blank -%}<div class="slabel reveal">{{ section.settings.lead_label }}</div>{%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="pf-lead-h reveal d1">{{ lead_heading }}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="pf-lead-b reveal d2">
      {%- if section.settings.lead_text != blank -%}<p class="pf-lead-p">{{ section.settings.lead_text | replace: count_token, total }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_lead_where and suburbs.size > 0 -%}
        <p class="pf-lead-where" aria-label="Suburbs">
          {%- for s in suburbs -%}{%- unless forloop.first %} <i>&middot;</i> {% endunless -%}<span>{{ s }}</span>{%- endfor -%}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if section.settings.show_filter and section.blocks.size > 3 -%}
{%- liquid
  assign style_n = styles.size
  if has_live
    assign style_n = style_n | plus: 1
  endif
  if has_sold
    assign style_n = style_n | plus: 1
  endif
  assign style_word = section.settings.filter_label | default: 'Style'
  assign all_styles = section.settings.filter_all | default: 'All'
  assign all_suburbs = section.settings.all_suburbs | default: 'All Suburbs'
  assign many_fallback = count_token | append: ' Styles'
  assign many_styles = section.settings.filter_many_styles | default: many_fallback
  assign many_fallback = count_token | append: ' Suburbs'
  assign many_suburbs = section.settings.filter_many_suburbs | default: many_fallback
-%}
<div class="pf-bar s-surface{% if section.settings.filter_sticky == false %} pf-static{% endif %}" data-pf-bar="{{ sid }}">
  <div class="inner pf-bar-inner">
    {%- comment -%} Style and Suburb side by side, each a dropdown with a box
        beside every choice so several can be ticked, the way Features works
        on For Sale (Naomi, 15 Sep 2026). {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="pf-chips pf-filters">
      {%- if style_n > 0 -%}
      <div class="pf-f">
        {%- if section.settings.filter_label != blank -%}<span class="pf-bar-l" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.settings.filter_label }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        <details class="pf-drop" id="pfStyle-{{ sid }}" data-pf-drop>
          <summary class="pf-sel pf-sel-drop"><span class="sr-only">{{ style_word }}: </span><span class="pf-sum" data-pf-summary data-pf-any="{{ all_styles | escape }}" data-pf-many="{{ many_styles | escape }}">{{ all_styles }}</span></summary>
          <div class="pf-menu" role="group" aria-label="{{ style_word | escape }}">
            {%- if has_live -%}<label class="pf-opt"><input type="checkbox" value="{{ live_word | escape }}" data-pf-opt="style" autocomplete="off"><span>{{ live_word }}</span></label>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if has_sold -%}<label class="pf-opt"><input type="checkbox" value="{{ sold_word | escape }}" data-pf-opt="style" autocomplete="off"><span>{{ sold_word }}</span></label>{%- endif -%}
            {%- for s in styles -%}<label class="pf-opt"><input type="checkbox" value="{{ s | escape }}" data-pf-opt="style" autocomplete="off"><span>{{ s }}</span></label>{%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if suburbs.size > 1 -%}
      <div class="pf-f">
        {%- if section.settings.suburb_label != blank -%}<span class="pf-bar-l" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.settings.suburb_label }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        <details class="pf-drop" id="pfSuburb-{{ sid }}" data-pf-drop>
          <summary class="pf-sel pf-sel-drop"><span class="sr-only">{{ section.settings.suburb_label | default: 'Suburb' }}: </span><span class="pf-sum" data-pf-summary data-pf-any="{{ all_suburbs | escape }}" data-pf-many="{{ many_suburbs | escape }}">{{ all_suburbs }}</span></summary>
          <div class="pf-menu" role="group" aria-label="{{ section.settings.suburb_label | default: 'Suburb' | escape }}">
            {%- for s in suburbs -%}<label class="pf-opt"><input type="checkbox" value="{{ s | escape }}" data-pf-opt="suburb" autocomplete="off"><span>{{ s }}</span></label>{%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <span class="pf-count" id="pfCount-{{ sid }}" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}

<section class="pf-wrap{% if section.settings.name_style == 'caps' %} pf-caps{% endif %}{% if section.settings.hover_zoom == false %} pf-nozoom{% endif %}" id="port-{{ sid }}" style="--pf-cols:{{ section.settings.columns | default: '3' }};--pf-ar:{{ section.settings.card_shape | default: '4/3' }};{% if section.settings.gap_y > 0 %}--pf-gap-y:{{ section.settings.gap_y }}px;{% endif %}{% if section.settings.gap_x > 0 %}--pf-gap-x:{{ section.settings.gap_x }}px;{% endif %}">
  <div class="inner">
    {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
      <p class="pf-intro reveal">{{ section.settings.intro | replace: count_token, total }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="pf-grid" id="pfGrid-{{ sid }}"{% if more_after > 0 %} data-pf-limit="{{ more_after }}"{% endif %}>
      {{- current_cards -}}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign rp = block.settings.page
          if rp == blank and block.settings.link contains '/pages/'
            assign rp_handle = block.settings.link | split: '/pages/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '#' | first
            assign rp = pages[rp_handle]
          endif
          # A residence that lives in Products (its own residence page and
          # Media folder, 14 Sep 2026) fills the card from the product; the
          # block's own fields still override.
          assign rprod = block.settings.product
        -%}
        {%- if rprod != blank -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign r_name = block.settings.name | default: rprod.title
          assign r_loc = block.settings.loc | default: rprod.metafields.custom.suburb.value
          assign r_suburb = r_loc | split: ',' | first | replace: ' QLD', '' | replace: ' Qld', '' | strip
          assign r_style = block.settings.style | default: rprod.metafields.custom.style.value | strip
          assign r_year = rprod.metafields.custom.year.value
          assign r_image_ext = block.settings.image_ext
          assign r_video = ''
          if tile_media == 'film'
            assign r_video = block.settings.video
            if block.settings.video_file
              assign pmp4 = block.settings.video_file.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4' | first
              if pmp4
                assign r_video = pmp4.url
              endif
            endif
            if r_video == blank
              for m in rprod.media
                if m.media_type == 'video'
                  assign own_mp4 = m.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4' | first
                  if own_mp4
                    assign r_video = own_mp4.url
                  endif
                  break
                endif
              endfor
            endif
          endif
          assign r_link = block.settings.link | default: rprod.url
          assign r_teaser = block.settings.teaser | default: rprod.metafields.custom.teaser.value
          if r_teaser == blank and rprod.metafields.custom.headline.value != blank
            assign r_teaser = rprod.metafields.custom.headline.value | strip_html
          endif
          assign r_beds = rprod.metafields.custom.beds.value
          assign r_baths = rprod.metafields.custom.baths.value
          assign r_land = rprod.metafields.custom.land.value
          assign pcount = pcount | plus: 1
          assign di = forloop.index0 | modulo: 3
          assign card_more = false
          if more_after > 0 and pcount > more_after
            assign card_more = true
          endif
        -%}
        {%- else -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign r_name = block.settings.name | default: rp.title
          assign r_loc = block.settings.loc | default: rp.metafields.custom.loc.value
          assign r_suburb = r_loc | split: ',' | first | replace: ' QLD', '' | replace: ' Qld', '' | strip
          assign r_style = block.settings.style | default: rp.metafields.custom.style.value | strip
          assign r_year = rp.metafields.custom.year.value
          assign r_image_ext = rp.metafields.custom.image.value | default: block.settings.image_ext
          if rp.metafields.custom.gallery.value.size > 0
            if r_image_ext == blank or r_image_ext contains '/films/' or r_image_ext contains '/images/'
              assign r_image_ext = rp.metafields.custom.gallery.value | first
            endif
          endif
          assign r_video = ''
          if tile_media == 'film'
            assign r_video = block.settings.video | default: rp.metafields.custom.video.value
            if block.settings.video_file
              assign pmp4 = block.settings.video_file.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4' | first
              if pmp4
                assign r_video = pmp4.url
              endif
            endif
          endif
          assign r_link = block.settings.link | default: rp.url
          # A small taste before the whole house: the Teaser line, else the
          # Headline, else the first strong Instagram caption, kept short.
          assign r_teaser = block.settings.teaser | default: rp.metafields.custom.teaser.value
          if r_teaser == blank and rp.metafields.custom.headline.value != blank
            assign r_teaser = rp.metafields.custom.headline.value | strip_html
          endif
          if r_teaser == blank
            for post in rp.metafields.custom.series_posts.value
              assign cap_l = post.caption | downcase
              assign skip = false
              if cap_l contains 'sold' or cap_l contains 'handed over'
                assign skip = true
              endif
              if post.caption.size > 60 and post.hidden != true and skip == false
                assign r_teaser = post.caption | strip_html | split: '. ' | first | split: ' - ' | first | split: ' — ' | first | split: ' – ' | first | truncatewords: 16, '…'
                break
              endif
            endfor
          endif
          assign r_beds = rp.metafields.custom.beds.value
          assign r_baths = rp.metafields.custom.baths.value
          assign r_land = rp.metafields.custom.land.value
          assign pcount = pcount | plus: 1
          assign di = forloop.index0 | modulo: 3
          assign card_more = false
          if more_after > 0 and pcount > more_after
            assign card_more = true
          endif
        -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- liquid
          # No photo anywhere (the block, the residence, its page): the card
          # keeps its name and details without an empty frame, and a block
          # with nothing chosen at all is left out (15 Sep 2026).
          assign pf_photo = false
          if block.settings.image or r_image_ext != blank
            assign pf_photo = true
          elsif rprod != blank and rprod.featured_image
            assign pf_photo = true
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if pf_photo == false and r_name == blank -%}{%- assign pcount = pcount | minus: 1 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- capture card_inner -%}
          {%- if pf_photo -%}
          <div class="pf-media">
            {%- if block.settings.image -%}
              <img src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1200, height: 900, crop: 'center' }}" alt="{{ r_name | escape }}{% if r_suburb != blank %}, {{ r_suburb | escape }}{% endif %}" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            {%- elsif rprod != blank and rprod.featured_image -%}
              <img src="{{ rprod.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200, height: 900, crop: 'center' }}" alt="{{ r_name | escape }}{% if r_suburb != blank %}, {{ r_suburb | escape }}{% endif %}" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            {%- elsif r_image_ext != blank -%}
              <img src="{% render 'ext-variant', src: r_image_ext, w: 1200, h: 900 %}" alt="{{ r_name | escape }}{% if r_suburb != blank %}, {{ r_suburb | escape }}{% endif %}" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if r_video != blank -%}
              <video src="{{ r_video }}" muted loop playsinline preload="none" data-port-video></video>
              {%- if section.settings.show_film_tag -%}<span class="port-film-tag">{{ section.settings.film_tag | default: "Film" }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if r_style != blank and section.settings.style_on_card -%}
              <span class="pf-style">{{ r_style }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="pf-info">
            <div class="pf-name">{{ r_name }}{% if r_link != blank and section.settings.show_arrow %} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>{% endif %}</div>
            {%- if section.settings.show_meta -%}<div class="pf-meta">{{ r_suburb }}{% if r_style != blank %} <i>&middot;</i> {{ r_style }}{% endif %}{% if r_year != blank %} <i>&middot;</i> {{ r_year }}{% endif %}</div>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
          {%- if section.settings.show_teaser and r_teaser != blank -%}
            <p class="pf-teaser">{{ r_teaser }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.show_facts -%}
            {%- if r_beds != blank or r_baths != blank or r_land != blank -%}
            <div class="pf-facts">
              {%- if r_beds != blank -%}<span>{{ r_beds }} {{ section.settings.word_bed | default: "Bed" }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if r_baths != blank -%}<span>{{ r_baths }} {{ section.settings.word_bath | default: "Bath" }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if r_land != blank -%}<span>{{ r_land }}{{ section.settings.unit_land }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if r_link != blank -%}
          <a href="{{ r_link }}" class="pf-card reveal{% if di == 1 %} d1{% elsif di == 2 %} d2{% endif %}{% if card_more %} pf-more{% endif %}" data-port-card data-style="{{ r_style | escape }}" data-suburb="{{ r_suburb | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ card_inner }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="pf-card reveal{% if di == 1 %} d1{% elsif di == 2 %} d2{% endif %}{% if card_more %} pf-more{% endif %}" data-port-card data-style="{{ r_style | escape }}" data-suburb="{{ r_suburb | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ card_inner }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    <p class="pf-empty" id="pfEmpty-{{ sid }}" hidden>{{ section.settings.empty_text }}</p>
    {%- if more_after > 0 and total > more_after -%}
      <div class="pf-more-row">
        <button type="button" class="btn-g pf-more-btn" id="pfMore-{{ sid }}" aria-controls="pfGrid-{{ sid }}">{{ section.settings.show_more_label | default: "Show more residences" }} <span class="pf-more-n" data-pf-more-n>{{ total | minus: more_after }}</span></button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Intro band: label, heading and the line about the houses on the left;
     the one-paragraph voice line and the suburbs present on the right. */
  .pf-lead{padding:calc(clamp(56px,7vw,96px)*var(--sp-scale)*var(--sp-top,1)) var(--page-pad) clamp(36px,4.5vw,60px);background:var(--bg)}
  .pf-lead-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:7fr 5fr;gap:clamp(32px,6vw,96px);align-items:end}
  .pf-lead-h{font-family:var(--font-d);font-size:calc(clamp(34px,4vw,60px)*var(--s-h,1));font-weight:300;line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--ink);margin:0;max-width:14ch}
  .pf-lead-h em{font-style:italic;color:var(--ink)}
  .pf-lead-p{font-size:calc(var(--t-body)*var(--s-t,1));font-weight:300;line-height:var(--lh-body);color:var(--ink3);margin:0;max-width:44ch}
  .pf-lead-where{font-family:var(--font-u);font-size:var(--t-label);font-weight:300;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--taupe-d);margin:18px 0 0;line-height:2}
  .pf-lead-where i{font-style:normal;color:var(--gold);margin:0 2px}
  .pf-lead-where span{white-space:nowrap}

  /* Filter bar: pinned to the nav's live height (--pf-top is set from
     #mainNav's measured height, so 80 / 68 / 60 / 56 all land flush), a
     near-solid cream over blur so tiles never show through, one hairline
     below, and always beneath the nav (nav is z 1000). */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-bar{position:sticky;top:var(--pf-top,var(--nav-h));z-index:20;padding:16px var(--page-pad);background:rgba(var(--bg-rgb),.96)!important;backdrop-filter:blur(14px);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-bar.pf-static{position:relative;top:auto}
  .pf-bar-inner{gap:20px 28px}
  .pf-count{white-space:nowrap}

  /* Style and Suburb together at the left, a small gap between, the count
     at the far right. Each is a dropdown with a tick box beside every
     choice (the For Sale Features menu, in this bar's own type and
     colours). The bar is positioned whenever it is not sticky (relative,
     not static) so an open list always lies over the grid. */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-filters{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px clamp(26px,3vw,40px);min-width:0}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-f{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;min-width:0}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-f .pf-bar-l{margin-right:0}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-count{margin-left:auto}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop{position:relative;min-width:0}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop>summary{list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:center;margin-left:0;max-width:100%;white-space:nowrap;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop>summary::marker{content:''}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop>summary:focus{outline:none}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop>summary:focus-visible{outline:1px solid var(--gold);outline-offset:3px}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-drop[open]>summary{border-bottom-color:var(--gold)}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-sum{min-width:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-menu{position:absolute;top:calc(100% + 10px);left:0;z-index:30;min-width:232px;max-width:calc(100vw - 32px);max-height:62vh;overflow-y:auto;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);box-shadow:0 20px 44px -20px rgba(var(--dark-rgb),.35);padding:6px 0}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-opt{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;padding:9px 16px;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-u);font-size:11px;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink2);white-space:nowrap}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-opt:hover{background:var(--bg2);color:var(--ink)}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-opt input{width:13px;height:13px;accent-color:var(--gold);flex-shrink:0;margin:0}

  /* No stray space between the bar and the first row: the grid carries no
     top margin, the wrap keeps one small, constant breath under the bar
     (the Look "Space above" dial now belongs to the intro band). */
  #port-{{ sid }}.pf-wrap{padding-top:clamp(28px,3.5vw,44px)}
  #port-{{ sid }} .pf-grid{margin-top:0}
  #port-{{ sid }} .pf-intro{margin-top:0}

  /* Show more: the tiles past the limit are hidden before paint (js gate,
     so a browser without script still sees every residence). */
  html.js #port-{{ sid }} .pf-card.pf-more{display:none}
  .pf-more-row{display:flex;justify-content:center;margin-top:clamp(40px,5vw,64px)}
  .pf-more-btn{font-family:var(--font-u);background:none;cursor:pointer}
  .pf-more-btn[hidden]{display:none}
  .pf-more-n{font-size:var(--t-micro);letter-spacing:.2em;color:var(--gold);margin-left:2px}
  html:not(.js) .pf-more-row{display:none}

  @media(max-width:900px){
    .pf-lead{padding-bottom:clamp(28px,5vw,40px)}
    .pf-lead-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:22px;align-items:start}
    .pf-lead-h{max-width:none}
    .pf-lead-where span{white-space:normal}
    /* On phones and tablets the bar stays in flow (as designed). Style and
       Suburb share one row where there is room (tablets) and stack, each
       full width, on a phone. The second list opens from its right edge so
       it never runs off screen. */
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-bar{position:relative;top:auto}
    .pf-bar-inner{gap:12px 16px}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-filters{width:100%;gap:12px 22px}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-f{flex:1 1 150px}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-f .pf-drop{flex:1 1 auto}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-f .pf-drop>summary{width:100%}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-f+.pf-f .pf-menu{left:auto;right:0}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .pf-count{margin-left:0;min-width:0;text-align:left}
    #port-{{ sid }}.pf-wrap{padding-top:clamp(24px,5vw,32px)}
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    var sid = {{ sid | json }};
    var grid = document.getElementById('pfGrid-' + sid);
    if (!grid || grid.dataset.init) return;
    grid.dataset.init = '1';
    var cards = Array.prototype.slice.call(grid.querySelectorAll('[data-port-card]'));
    var bar = document.querySelector('[data-pf-bar="' + sid + '"]');
    var drops = bar ? Array.prototype.slice.call(bar.querySelectorAll('[data-pf-drop]')) : [];
    var boxes = bar ? Array.prototype.slice.call(bar.querySelectorAll('input[data-pf-opt]')) : [];
    var count = document.getElementById('pfCount-' + sid);
    var empty = document.getElementById('pfEmpty-' + sid);
    var more = document.getElementById('pfMore-' + sid);
    var moreN = more ? more.querySelector('[data-pf-more-n]') : null;
    var limit = parseInt(grid.getAttribute('data-pf-limit') || '0', 10) || 0;
    var expanded = false;
    var words = { one: {{ section.settings.count_one | default: 'Residence' | json }}, many: {{ section.settings.count_many | default: 'Residences' | json }}, of: {{ section.settings.count_of | default: 'of' | json }} };

    /* A choice and a card compare without capitals or doubled spaces, so
       "Camp Hill" on one page and "camp hill" on another are one suburb. */
    function norm(s) { return String(s || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim().toLowerCase(); }
    function ticked(kind) {
      return boxes.filter(function (b) { return b.checked && b.getAttribute('data-pf-opt') === kind; })
        .map(function (b) { return norm(b.value); });
    }

    /* One pass decides every tile: its style is one of the ticked styles
       (or none is ticked), its suburb one of the ticked suburbs (or none
       is), and it is inside the Show-more limit (or the limit is off, or
       the visitor has opened the rest). Filters search the whole set, so
       a choice that matches three houses shows all three. */
    function apply(initial) {
      var styles = ticked('style');
      var subs = ticked('suburb');
      var matched = 0, shown = 0;
      cards.forEach(function (c) {
        var ok = true;
        if (styles.length && styles.indexOf(norm(c.dataset.style)) === -1) ok = false;
        if (ok && subs.length && subs.indexOf(norm(c.dataset.suburb)) === -1) ok = false;
        if (ok) matched++;
        var show = ok && (expanded || !limit || matched <= limit);
        if (show) shown++;
        var was = !c.hidden && !c.classList.contains('pf-more');
        c.hidden = !show;
        c.classList.remove('pf-more');
        if (show && !initial) {
          if (!was) c.classList.add('fastin');
          c.classList.add('vis');
        }
      });
      var rest = matched - shown;
      if (empty) empty.hidden = matched > 0;
      if (more) {
        more.hidden = rest <= 0;
        if (moreN) moreN.textContent = rest;
      }
      if (count) {
        if (styles.length || subs.length) count.textContent = matched + ' ' + (matched === 1 ? words.one : words.many);
        else if (rest > 0) count.textContent = shown + ' ' + words.of + ' ' + matched;
        else count.textContent = '';
      }
    }

    /* Each dropdown names what is ticked: nothing (All), the one choice,
       or how many. */
    function label(drop) {
      var out = drop.querySelector('[data-pf-summary]');
      if (!out) return;
      var on = Array.prototype.filter.call(drop.querySelectorAll('input[data-pf-opt]'), function (b) { return b.checked; });
      if (!on.length) out.textContent = out.getAttribute('data-pf-any') || '';
      else if (on.length === 1) out.textContent = on[0].parentNode.textContent.trim();
      else out.textContent = (out.getAttribute('data-pf-many') || '{count}').replace('{count}', on.length);
    }
    boxes.forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener('change', function () {
        var d = b.closest('[data-pf-drop]');
        if (d) label(d);
        apply();
      });
    });
    drops.forEach(function (d) {
      label(d);
      /* One list open at a time. */
      d.addEventListener('toggle', function () {
        if (d.open) drops.forEach(function (o) { if (o !== d) o.open = false; });
      });
    });
    /* A list left open over the grid gets in the way: a click anywhere
       else, or Escape, closes it. */
    if (drops.length) {
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        drops.forEach(function (d) { if (d.open && !d.contains(e.target)) d.open = false; });
      });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key !== 'Escape') return;
        drops.forEach(function (d) {
          if (!d.open) return;
          d.open = false;
          if (d.isConnected) d.querySelector('summary').focus();
        });
      });
    }
    if (more) more.addEventListener('click', function () { expanded = true; apply(); });
    apply(true);

    /* Pin the bar to the nav's live height. The nav shrinks from 80px to
       68px once the page has scrolled (60 / 56 on phones), so a fixed
       top: var(--nav-h) left a strip between the two. */
    var nav = document.getElementById('mainNav');
    if (bar && nav) {
      var setTop = function () {
        bar.style.setProperty('--pf-top', Math.round(nav.getBoundingClientRect().height) + 'px');
      };
      setTop();
      if ('ResizeObserver' in window) {
        new ResizeObserver(setTop).observe(nav);
      } else {
        window.addEventListener('scroll', setTop, { passive: true });
        window.addEventListener('resize', setTop);
      }
    }
    {%- if tile_media == 'film' %}
    if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    cards.forEach(function (card) {
      var video = card.querySelector('[data-port-video]');
      if (!video) return;
      card.addEventListener('mouseenter', function () { video.play().then(function () { video.classList.add('playing'); }).catch(function () {}); });
      card.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { video.pause(); video.classList.remove('playing'); });
    });
    {%- endif %}
  })();
</script>


{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection grid",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Completed residences only. Homes for sale live on their own page (For Sale); nothing from Products appears here. Add one Residence block per completed home and pick its page - the card fills itself from that page's metafields (Content › Pages › the residence › Metafields: Style, Completed year, Hero image, Film)." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Intro band" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_lead", "label": "Show the intro band above the filter bar", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lead_label", "label": "Small label", "default": "The Collection" },
    { "type": "html", "id": "lead_heading", "label": "Heading (HTML - <em> allowed)", "default": "Completed residences, <em>{count} and counting</em>.", "info": "{count} becomes the number of residences on this page." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lead_text", "label": "One paragraph", "default": "Every residence here was drawn, developed and built by Sabdia, in inner Brisbane, and handed over complete." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_lead_where", "label": "List the suburbs present", "default": true, "info": "Drawn from each residence page's Location line, one entry per suburb." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Filter bar" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_filter", "label": "Show the filter bar", "default": true, "info": "Style and Suburb dropdowns side by side, each with a tick box beside every choice so visitors can pick several. Styles come from each residence page's Style field, suburbs from its Location line; every value on the page is listed once, A to Z. Appears once there are four or more residences." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "style_on_card", "label": "Show the style on the photo on hover", "default": true },
    { "type": "header", "content": "A taste before the whole house" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "intro", "label": "Optional line above the grid", "info": "Sits between the filter bar and the first row. {count} becomes the number of residences. Empty (as designed) hides it; the intro band above carries the count." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_teaser", "label": "One-line teaser under each name", "default": true, "info": "From the page's Teaser line (Content › Pages › the residence › Metafields), else its Headline, else its first Instagram caption." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_facts", "label": "Bed · bath · land under the teaser", "default": true, "info": "Shows whatever the page has filled in." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "word_bed", "label": "Word after bedrooms", "default": "Bed" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "word_bath", "label": "Word after bathrooms", "default": "Bath" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "unit_land", "label": "Land size unit", "default": "m²", "info": "Straight after the land size, e.g. 405m²." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_label", "label": "Style label", "default": "Style", "info": "The small label before the style dropdown." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_all", "label": "Style dropdown, nothing ticked", "default": "All" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_many_styles", "label": "Style dropdown, several ticked", "default": "{count} Styles", "info": "{count} becomes the number of styles ticked. One ticked shows its name." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "suburb_label", "label": "Suburb label (optional)", "info": "A small label before the suburb dropdown, like Style before the style one. Empty shows the wording below alone." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "all_suburbs", "label": "Suburb dropdown, nothing ticked", "default": "All Suburbs" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_many_suburbs", "label": "Suburb dropdown, several ticked", "default": "{count} Suburbs", "info": "{count} becomes the number of suburbs ticked. One ticked shows its name." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_text", "label": "No-matches text", "default": "Nothing matches those filters. Try widening them." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_one", "label": "Count while filtering - one residence", "default": "Residence", "info": "At the right of the filter bar once a filter is ticked, e.g. 1 Residence." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_many", "label": "Count while filtering - several residences", "default": "Residences", "info": "e.g. 3 Residences." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_of", "label": "Count with Show more - word between the numbers", "default": "of", "info": "e.g. 12 of 20, while some tiles wait behind the Show more button." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "film_tag", "label": "Film tag", "default": "Film" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Many residences" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_more", "label": "Show more button after the first tiles", "default": false, "info": "Keeps the page quick as the collection grows: the first tiles load, a button reveals the rest in place. Filters always search every residence." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "show_more_after", "label": "Tiles shown before the button", "min": 6, "max": 36, "step": 3, "default": 12 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "show_more_label", "label": "Button wording", "default": "Show more residences", "info": "The number still to come follows the wording." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Residences from Products (For Sale / Sold)" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_current", "label": "Include residences from Products", "default": false, "info": "Off since 10 Sep 2026 (Tamsin): For Sale has its own page. On = the current homes lead the grid, tagged by their Status, with For Sale / Sold filter chips." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "current_scope", "label": "Which ones", "options": [ { "value": "sold", "label": "Sold only (past projects)" }, { "value": "all", "label": "For Sale and Sold" } ], "default": "all" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_live", "label": "For Sale chip", "default": "For Sale" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "filter_sold", "label": "Sold chip", "default": "Sold" },
    {"type": "header", "content": "Cards"},
    {"type": "select", "id": "tile_media", "label": "Tile media", "options": [{"value": "photo", "label": "Photo only (as designed)"}, {"value": "film", "label": "Film on hover"}], "default": "photo", "info": "Photo only keeps the page light; each residence's film plays on its own page. Film on hover needs a Film on the residence page or block."},
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "show_film_tag", "label": "Film tag on cards that have one", "default": true, "info": "Only with Film on hover."},
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "show_arrow", "label": "Arrow after each name", "default": true},
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "show_meta", "label": "Suburb · style · year under each name", "default": true},
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "hover_zoom", "label": "Photos zoom gently on hover", "default": true},
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "filter_sticky", "label": "Filter bar sticks under the nav while scrolling", "default": true, "info": "On phones the bar stays in flow either way."},
    {"type": "select", "id": "name_style", "label": "Name style", "options": [{"value": "serif", "label": "Serif (as designed)"}, {"value": "caps", "label": "Small tracked capitals"}], "default": "serif"},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Layout"},
    {"type": "select", "id": "columns", "label": "Cards across", "options": [{"value": "2", "label": "Two"}, {"value": "3", "label": "Three (as designed)"}, {"value": "4", "label": "Four"}], "default": "3"},
    {"type": "select", "id": "card_shape", "label": "Card shape", "options": [{"value": "16/10", "label": "Landscape 16:10"}, {"value": "4/3", "label": "Landscape 4:3"}, {"value": "3/2", "label": "Landscape 3:2"}, {"value": "16/9", "label": "Wide 16:9"}, {"value": "1/1", "label": "Square"}, {"value": "4/5", "label": "Portrait 4:5"}], "default": "4/3"},
    {"type": "range", "id": "gap_y", "label": "Gap between rows", "min": 0, "max": 80, "step": 4, "default": 0, "unit": "px", "info": "0 = as designed (grows with the window)."},
    {"type": "range", "id": "gap_x", "label": "Gap between columns", "min": 0, "max": 60, "step": 4, "default": 0, "unit": "px", "info": "0 = as designed (grows with the window)."},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Look"},
    {"type": "paragraph", "content": "The same dials the home hero has, for this section. Leave everything as designed and nothing changes; every dial is undoable."},
    {"type": "select", "id": "look_surface", "label": "Background", "options": [{"value": "design", "label": "As designed"}, {"value": "cream", "label": "Cream (the page colour)"}, {"value": "stone", "label": "Stone (soft panel)"}, {"value": "obsidian", "label": "Obsidian (dark)"}, {"value": "custom", "label": "A colour of your own (below)"}, {"value": "media", "label": "A photo or film behind it (below)"}], "default": "design", "info": "Obsidian turns the words light; cream and stone keep them dark. Buttons, rules, panels and cards follow the surface."},
    {"type": "color", "id": "look_color", "label": "Your colour", "default": "#F0EADE", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'custom' }}"},
    {"type": "select", "id": "look_tone", "label": "Words on your colour", "options": [{"value": "light", "label": "Dark words (for a light colour)"}, {"value": "dark", "label": "Light words (for a dark colour)"}], "default": "light", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'custom' }}"},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Backdrop photo or film", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "paragraph", "content": "A backdrop behind this section's words, used only while Background is a photo or film. It is not the residence film. Real photographs and real footage only, never generated.", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "image_picker", "id": "look_image", "label": "Backdrop photo", "info": "Also the poster while a backdrop film loads.", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "video", "id": "look_video", "label": "Backdrop film (upload)", "info": "Plays silently on a loop. Landscape 16:9, under 20 MB keeps the page fast.", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "look_media_link", "label": "Use a film link instead of an upload", "default": false, "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "look_video_url", "label": "Backdrop film (URL)", "info": "A direct .mp4 link, used when no backdrop film is uploaded above.", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' and section.settings.look_media_link }}"},
    {"type": "range", "id": "look_dim", "label": "Darken the backdrop", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 55, "info": "Lower = brighter. The words stay readable down to about 40%.", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "select", "id": "look_focus", "label": "Backdrop crop focus", "options": [{"value": "center", "label": "Centre"}, {"value": "top", "label": "Top"}, {"value": "bottom", "label": "Bottom"}, {"value": "left", "label": "Left"}, {"value": "right", "label": "Right"}], "default": "center", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "select", "id": "look_media_tone", "label": "Words over the backdrop", "options": [{"value": "dark", "label": "Light words on a darkened backdrop"}, {"value": "light", "label": "Dark words on a pale backdrop"}], "default": "dark", "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.look_surface == 'media' }}"},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Space"},
    {"type": "range", "id": "look_space_top", "label": "Space above", "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 10, "unit": "%", "default": 100, "info": "100 = as designed. Theme settings › Layout › Space above and below sections still scales the whole site; this dial is for this section only."},
    {"type": "range", "id": "look_space_bottom", "label": "Space below", "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 10, "unit": "%", "default": 100},
    {"type": "select", "id": "look_width", "label": "Content width", "options": [{"value": "theme", "label": "Theme setting (Layout › Content width)"}, {"value": "720", "label": "Narrow (720px)"}, {"value": "900", "label": "Reading (900px)"}, {"value": "1100", "label": "Medium (1100px)"}, {"value": "1300", "label": "Wide (1300px)"}, {"value": "1600", "label": "Very wide (1600px)"}, {"value": "edge", "label": "Edge to edge"}], "default": "theme"},
    {"type": "range", "id": "look_margins", "label": "Side margins", "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 10, "unit": "%", "default": 100, "info": "A share of the site's side margins (Theme settings › Layout). 0 runs to the edges."},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Type"},
    {"type": "range", "id": "look_heading", "label": "Heading size", "min": 50, "max": 160, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 100, "info": "Scales the serif headings and titles in this section."},
    {"type": "range", "id": "look_text", "label": "Text size", "min": 70, "max": 140, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 100, "info": "Paragraphs, captions and standfirsts."},
